<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Brand launcher mark: the Exhale "E))" (assets/icon.png).

    The source art is already an app-icon-shaped tile — a black glyph on a gold squircle — and an
    adaptive icon must NOT be handed one of those whole. Doing so draws a squircle inside the
    launcher's own squircle, and insetting it into the 72dp safe zone instead leaves the tile's
    edge floating as a visible plate on top of the background layer. Both read as a sticker
    rather than as an icon.

    So the tile is split along its own seams: the gold is the BACKGROUND layer, full-bleed, and
    the glyph alone — carrying its rim light, shading and drop shadow — is the FOREGROUND, scaled
    to 62% of the layer so it clears the safe zone under every mask. There is no plate edge left
    to show, and the launcher masks gold at whatever shape it likes.

    All three layers are per-density PNGs generated together from assets/icon.png; regenerate
    them as a set, never by hand. NOTE: distinct from the splash mark (@drawable/splash_logo) —
    do not conflate them.
-->
<adaptive-icon xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">
    <background android:drawable="@mipmap/ic_launcher_background" />
    <foreground android:drawable="@mipmap/ic_launcher_foreground" />
    <monochrome android:drawable="@mipmap/ic_launcher_monochrome" />
</adaptive-icon>
